A||||10||GWMORGAN||Could It Be The Chip?||||1
Z||000000||GWMORGAN||10-09-1999||08:12 PM||||I replaced the stock chip on my 86 v6 GT 5 spd. with an ADS "Street Runner" performance chip and have seen the idle go from 900-1000 rpm to 1200-1300 rpm when warm. Is this normal? I run preminm grade gas and average 32-35 mpg. Is it that the timing is advance by the chip, and if so, can the correct timing be set with the ADS chip?<BR>BTW, I have a 160 degree stat and fan switch installed. The info will be appreciated. Thanks. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||mwbackus||10-09-1999||08:31 PM||||The ADS "Street Runner" chip was not designed to be used with a 160° system.  The Hypertech Thermomaster is the chip that was designed for this, and it is the only reason that the 160° system (stat and fan switch) is even available.  Your ECM is detecting the low temperature operation and reacting accordingly by staying in open loop mode.  I would suggest either switching to a 180° stat, or obtaining a Thermomaster chip.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000002||GWMORGAN||10-09-1999||08:44 PM||||mwbckus,<BR>       If I use a 180 degree stat. do I have to change the fan switch also??<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||10-09-1999||09:13 PM||||You are getting 32 mpg with v6 and a chip? That is pretty good considering my 4cyl gets 30 mpg and has no power at all.||||reg||5
Z||000004||GWMORGAN||10-09-1999||09:51 PM||||cooter,<BR>      That's right, I average 320-350 miles on 10.3 gallons petrol. Driverbility of the car is not sacrificed with the ADS street chip (one of the claims they make).BTW, the car is well tuned;with 178,000 miles on the motor and I'm also running a MSD 6a ignition box and coil. That has a lot to do with the performance of the car.||||reg||1
Z||000005||mwbackus||10-09-1999||11:04 PM||||It is my understanding, that one can get by just fine with a low temp (176°) fan switch and a 180° stat.  In fact, I think its probably the best system to use on the V6.  The 4° difference would be just about right, starting the fan just prior to the stat opening.  The 180° operation has been confirmed as "OK" on the L4 by one of our most prestigious members, so I would assume that it would also be acceptable on the V6.  I have not found the 180° stat to be easily obtained, since, they are considered "special orders" by my local parts hangouts, so I would be interested if you find a good supplier.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000006||WisconsinGT||10-10-1999||12:32 AM||||I have a 180 degree stat in my 88V6. All is well. For what it's worth, I am getting about 270-290 miles on a tank of gas.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Bruce||10-10-1999||01:16 AM||||I have the ADS chip and the stock teperature thermostat, and my Fiero runs great. Any precautionary responses? I've never really worried about the mileage, since I just drive it the car on the weekends.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Bruce||10-10-1999||01:17 AM||||I have the ADS chip and the stock teperature thermostat, and my Fiero runs great. Any precautionary responses? I've never really worried about the mileage, since I just drive it the car on the weekends.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Lynx||10-10-1999||02:21 AM||||I have the 180 thermostat in my 85 4cyl and it works perfect no longer gets to hot in town unless you sit for a long time and it works real well to keep it at a perfect temp on the freeway which increased my mileage. Also if you have a problem getting the thermostat i can get it easy at my local part store. They stock it and it was under $10 (like $6.99 or $8.99). So if you have a prob i can get you one.||||reg||7
Z||000010||GWMORGAN||10-10-1999||03:12 PM||||Thanks for the offer Lynx....If I can't get the stat. locally I will contact you by email. Is it one stat. for both motors?||||reg||1
